BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Istanbul//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-01@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Simit
DESCRIPTION:Say it: see-MEET. Le préféré du chef. The sesame bread ring\, dipped in grape molasses before the seeds go on — that is the dark lacquer. Why it matters: Ottoman price registers had it in Istanbul by 1525\; the state fixed its weight by decree because too many people lived off it. Best place: Off the tray on the Eminönü–Kadıköy vapur. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Off the tray on the Eminönü–Kadıköy vapur
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-02@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Serpme kahvaltı
DESCRIPTION:Say it: SERP-meh kah-vahl-TUH. Le préféré du chef. The sprawled Sunday breakfast — twenty small plates\, three hours\, tables held rather than turned. You get to taste everything at once. Why it matters: Kahvaltı means "before coffee": the biggest meal of the Turkish day is named for the drink it precedes. Best place: Van Kahvaltı Evi\, Cihangir — Sunday\, go early. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Van%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Evi%20Cihangir%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Van Kahvaltı Evi\, Cihangir — Sunday\, go early
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Van%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Evi%20Cihangir%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-03@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Muhammara
DESCRIPTION:Say it: moo-hahm-mah-RAH. Le préféré du chef. Walnuts\, red-pepper paste and pomegranate molasses pounded into a coarse paste — on the breakfast spread and the meze tray both. Why it matters: The Hatay–Aleppo table in one bowl: the south-eastern half of the city's cooking\, spread on bread before nine in the morning. Best place: On the serpme spread\, or at an Antakya house — Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
LOCATION:On the serpme spread\, or at an Antakya house — Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-04@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Menemen
DESCRIPTION:Say it: meh-neh-MEN. Le préféré du chef. Eggs scrambled loosely into tomato and green pepper\, eaten from the pan with bread — the Turkish cousin of shakshuka. Why it matters: Turkey's great breakfast argument: with onion or without (soğanlı / soğansız) genuinely divides the country. Order it and take a side. Best place: Çakmak Kahvaltı Salonu\, Beşiktaş. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87akmak%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Salonu%20Be%C5%9Fikta%C5%9F%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Çakmak Kahvaltı Salonu\, Beşiktaş
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87akmak%20Kahvalt%C4%B1%20Salonu%20Be%C5%9Fikta%C5%9F%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-05@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Yaprak sarma
DESCRIPTION:Say it: yah-PRAHK sahr-MAH. Le préféré du chef. Vine leaves rolled thin as a finger around rice\, herbs and spice\, eaten cold with a squeeze of lemon. The good ones\, mind — hand-rolled\, tight\, no shortcuts. Why it matters: The zeytinyağlı register — the palace half of the table: vegetables cooked in olive oil and served cold\, restraint as a cuisine. Best place: The zeytinyağlı trays at Çiya Sofrası\, Kadıköy. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87iya%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:The zeytinyağlı trays at Çiya Sofrası\, Kadıköy
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%C3%87iya%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-06@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Mercimek çorbası
DESCRIPTION:Say it: mehr-jee-MEK chor-bah-SUH. Le préféré du chef. Red lentil soup — and the ritual matters: fresh lemon squeezed in\, pul biber on top. Never skip either. Why it matters: The most democratic dish in Turkey: every lokanta opens with it\, every taxi driver has an opinion on it\, and it costs almost nothing. Best place: Yanyalı Fehmi Lokantası\, Kadıköy — trading since 1919. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yanyal%C4%B1%20Fehmi%20Lokantas%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Yanyalı Fehmi Lokantası\, Kadıköy — trading since 1919
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yanyal%C4%B1%20Fehmi%20Lokantas%C4%B1%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-07@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Çiğ köfte
DESCRIPTION:Say it: CHEE kuf-TEH. Le préféré du chef. Fine bulgur kneaded for hours with pepper paste and a dozen spices\, wrapped in lettuce with lemon — a "tartare" of grain. Why it matters: The name means raw meatball and it no longer contains any: the street version went meatless by regulation\, and the knead survived the meat. Best place: Bezirgan Çiğ Köfte Salonu\, Kadıköy — call ahead. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bezirgan%20%C3%87i%C4%9F%20K%C3%B6fte%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Bezirgan Çiğ Köfte Salonu\, Kadıköy — call ahead
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bezirgan%20%C3%87i%C4%9F%20K%C3%B6fte%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-08@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Balık ekmek
DESCRIPTION:Say it: bah-LUHK ek-MEK. Le préféré du chef. Grilled fish in a half loaf\, eaten standing by the water. Why it matters: No inventor and no founding date — it is what happens when a fishing fleet ties up at the foot of a hungry city. Best place: The Karaköy waterfront counters — not the painted Eminönü boats. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=bal%C4%B1k%20ekmek%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:The Karaköy waterfront counters — not the painted Eminönü boats
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=bal%C4%B1k%20ekmek%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-09@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Turşu — the pickles
DESCRIPTION:Say it: toor-SHOO. Le préféré du chef. Cucumber\, cabbage\, beet\, green plum — pickled sharp\, sold from barrels\, the brine drunk by the glass as turşu suyu. Why it matters: The turşucu is a shop that sells nothing else\, and has not needed to for a century. Drink the juice: it is the point. Best place: A turşucu in the Kadıköy çarşı. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=tur%C5%9Fucu%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:A turşucu in the Kadıköy çarşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=tur%C5%9Fucu%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-10@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Ayran
DESCRIPTION:Say it: eye-RAHN. Le préféré du chef. Salted yoghurt whipped thin\, best from the churn (yayık) with a collar of foam. Why it matters: A confession: the house hates it. It is still a must — no kebab is complete without the glass beside it\, and Turkey drinks more of it than anything else. Best place: From the yayık wherever you sit at a fire — Tam Ocakbaşı. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:From the yayık wherever you sit at a fire — Tam Ocakbaşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-11@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Midye dolma
DESCRIPTION:Say it: MEED-yeh DOHL-mah. Mussels stuffed with spiced rice\, sold from trays after dark\, one lemon squeeze per shell. Why it matters: An Armenian dish before it was an Istanbul one — recorded in an 1888 yearbook\, made with large mussels and sheep-tail fat. Best place: Midyeci Ahmet\, Karaköy. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Midyeci%20Ahmet%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Midyeci Ahmet\, Karaköy
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Midyeci%20Ahmet%20Karak%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-12@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Ciğer at the ocakbaşı
DESCRIPTION:Say it: jee-EHR at the oh-jak-bah-SHUH. Liver first\, then the skewers\, a lahmacun to close — you sit at the charcoal trench and the cook works in front of you. Why it matters: The most Istanbul way to eat fire: the ocakbaşı is a bar with a grill in it\, carried north by south-eastern migration. Best place: Tam Ocakbaşı\, Arnavutköy — book for Friday or Saturday. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Tam Ocakbaşı\, Arnavutköy — book for Friday or Saturday
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tam%20Ocakba%C5%9F%C4%B1%20Arnavutk%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-13@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Fıstıklı kuru baklava
DESCRIPTION:Say it: fuhs-tuhk-LUH koo-ROO bahk-lah-VAH. The dry pistachio baklava — no cream\, cut small\, bought by weight. Why it matters: The Güllü family carried the craft from Damascus to Gaziantep in 1871\; the dry version survives being carried onto a boat. Best place: Karaköy Güllüoğlu — open past midnight. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Karak%C3%B6y%20G%C3%BCll%C3%BCo%C4%9Flu%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Karaköy Güllüoğlu — open past midnight
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Karak%C3%B6y%20G%C3%BCll%C3%BCo%C4%9Flu%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-14@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Künefe
DESCRIPTION:Say it: kew-neh-FEH. Shredded pastry over molten cheese\, cooked to order and eaten hot — it does not wait for you. Why it matters: Antakya's dessert\, made properly in Istanbul by houses that came north from Hatay. Best place: Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası\, off İstiklal. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Hatay Medeniyetler Sofrası\, off İstiklal
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatay%20Medeniyetler%20Sofras%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-15@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Boza
DESCRIPTION:Say it: BOH-zah. Fermented millet\, thick and faintly sour\, with cinnamon and roasted chickpeas on top. Winter only — it spoils in heat. Why it matters: Vefa Bozacısı has poured it since 1876 in a room that has barely changed\; the only shop of its generation still trading. Best place: Vefa Bozacısı\, Fatih. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vefa%20Bozac%C4%B1s%C4%B1%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Vefa Bozacısı\, Fatih
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Vefa%20Bozac%C4%B1s%C4%B1%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-16@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Türk kahvesi
DESCRIPTION:Say it: tewrk kah-veh-SEE. Coffee milled finer than espresso\, brought up slowly in the cezve and never allowed to boil — judge it by the foam. Why it matters: The word kahvaltı itself bows to this cup: everything eaten before it is just preparation. Best place: Fazıl Bey\, Kadıköy çarşı. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Faz%C4%B1l%20Bey%20T%C3%BCrk%20Kahvesi%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Fazıl Bey\, Kadıköy çarşı
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Faz%C4%B1l%20Bey%20T%C3%BCrk%20Kahvesi%20Kad%C4%B1k%C3%B6y%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-17@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Çay on the ferry deck
DESCRIPTION:Say it: CHAI. Tea in a tulip glass from the tray that never spills\, on the open deck mid-strait. Why it matters: Twenty minutes\, the price of a bus ride\, and the best view in the city is included. Best place: Any Şehir Hatları vapur — take the aft deck. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Any Şehir Hatları vapur — take the aft deck
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Emin%C3%B6n%C3%BC%20Ferry%20Pier%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-18@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Rakı-balık
DESCRIPTION:Say it: rah-KUH bah-LUHK. The full meyhane night: cold mezes\, then hot\, then one fish — chosen off the ice by the door and weighed in front of you\, never off a menu. Why it matters: The meyhane table was built by the city's Greeks\, Armenians and Jews\; the ritual outlived its authors. Best place: Agora Meyhanesi 1890\, Balat. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Agora%20Meyhanesi%201890%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Agora Meyhanesi 1890\, Balat
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Agora%20Meyhanesi%201890%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-19@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Tavuk göğsü
DESCRIPTION:Say it: tah-VOOK goess-SUE. A milk pudding thickened with chicken breast pulled so fine you cannot find it — sweet\, not savoury. Why it matters: A palace dessert a patisserie cannot make\; order it where a muhallebici still exists to make it. Best place: Saray Muhallebicisi\, İstiklal. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Saray%20Muhallebicisi%20%C4%B0stiklal%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Saray Muhallebicisi\, İstiklal
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Saray%20Muhallebicisi%20%C4%B0stiklal%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-20@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:İşkembe soup
DESCRIPTION:Say it: eesh-kem-BEH. Tripe soup\, garlic vinegar on top\, taken after midnight against the rakı. Why it matters: The city's licensed cure: işkembeci keep the hours the meyhane makes necessary. Best place: Lale İşkembecisi\, Tarlabaşı — since 1965. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lale%20%C4%B0%C5%9Fkembecisi%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Lale İşkembecisi\, Tarlabaşı — since 1965
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lale%20%C4%B0%C5%9Fkembecisi%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-21@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Öküzgözü
DESCRIPTION:Say it: oh-kooz-goh-ZOO. The juicy\, dark-fruited Anatolian red — the name means "ox eye"\, after the size of the berries. Why it matters: One of the indigenous grapes almost nobody outside Turkey orders — which is exactly why to order it here. Best place: Solera Winery\, Tomtom. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Solera%20Winery%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Solera Winery\, Tomtom
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Solera%20Winery%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-22@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Boğazkere
DESCRIPTION:Say it: boh-ahz-keh-REH. The tannic Anatolian red — the name means "throat burner". Built for lamb off the fire. Why it matters: Drink it at an ocakbaşı and the pairing explains both the grape and the grill. Best place: Sensus Wine Boutique\, Galata. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sensus%20Wine%20Boutique%20Istanbul
LOCATION:Sensus Wine Boutique\, Galata
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sensus%20Wine%20Boutique%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:terroir-ist-checklist-23@littoralicious.com
DTSTAMP:20260817T160000Z
SUMMARY:Narince & Emir
DESCRIPTION:Say it: nah-rin-DJEH · eh-MEER. The Anatolian whites\, cold: Narince from Tokat\, Emir from Cappadocia. Why it matters: Grown on some of the oldest wine ground on earth\, and still barely exported. Best place: WAYANA Wine Bar\, Karaköy — natural list. Map: https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=WAYANA%20Wine%20Bar%20Istanbul
LOCATION:WAYANA Wine Bar\, Karaköy — natural list
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=WAYANA%20Wine%20Bar%20Istanbul
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
